<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Untitled Document</title>
    <style>
        body { 
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif; 
            margin: 0; 
            padding: 0; 
            display: flex; 
            justify-content: center; 
            align-items: center; 
            min-height: 100vh; 
            background: #f9f9f9; 
            color: #000; 
        }
        .document-container {
            width: 800px;
            max-width: 100%;
            padding: 40px 30px;
            box-sizing: border-box;
            position: relative;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            background: white;
            box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }
        .placeholder {
            width: 200px;
            height: 150px;
            background: #f0f0f0;
            border: 1px solid #aaa;
            margin: 10px 0;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            font-size: 12px;
            color: #666;
            text-align: center;
        }
        .placeholder::before {
            content: "[Placeholder image / Diagram]";
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="document-container">
        <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;">
            <strong>Sample Document Header</strong>
        </div>

        <!-- Main body text zone -->
        <p style="margin: 12px 0; text-align: justify;">This is the first paragraph of the document. It demonstrates how the OCR-to-HTML converter would render the text block in a single column layout with justified alignment and standard paragraph spacing.</p>

        <p style="margin: 12px 0; text-align: justify;">The second paragraph continues the body content. Spatial fidelity is maintained by preserving the exact left and right margins as they would appear in the original scanned image.</p>

        <div class="placeholder" style="margin: 20px 0; width: 300px; height: 200px;"></div>

        <p style="margin: 12px 0; text-align: justify;">Any charts, diagrams, or images present in the source document are replaced with a placeholder element that matches the visual footprint and position exactly as they appeared on the page.</p>

        <ul style="margin: 15px 0 15px 30px; list-style-type: disc;">
            <li>Bullet point one from the original document.</li>
            <li>Bullet point two appears here with the same indentation and spacing.</li>
            <li>This list maintains the exact vertical positioning seen in the scanned layout.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="placeholder" style="margin: 30px auto; width: 250px; height: 180px;"></div>

        <p style="margin: 12px 0; text-align: justify;">Footer text or additional sections would be rendered at the bottom of the page with the same font size and spacing as the body content.</p>

        <div style="margin-top: 40px; text-align: center; font-size: 10px; color: #888;">
            [illegible] [Placeholder] [Diagram]
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
